Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Biomolecular Condensates and the Origin of Life", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"3041e4e1-a69e-4fb8-b9db-a4a4afb50505"],

Cell["\<\
From Flory\[Dash]Huggins thermodynamics to protocellular compartments \
\[LongDash] first-principles mathematical modelling of liquid\[Dash]liquid \
phase separation in biology\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"a136883d-cd1a-494e-b42e-7e79f76f390c"],

Cell["Marco Thiel", "Subsubtitle",
 FontSlant->Italic,ExpressionUUID->"1d0f882f-6d5d-4bc3-8907-5afd58fd0edb"],

Cell["Wolfram Community post \[LongDash] June 2026", "Subsubtitle",
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.4],ExpressionUUID->"25fb2196-aba9-456b-8be1-6bc771c91d84"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Abstract", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dc156eab-7162-441a-ad8d-0b953098f82b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Biomolecular condensates are ",
 StyleBox["membrane-free liquid droplets",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " inside cells, formed by liquid\[Dash]liquid phase separation (LLPS) of \
proteins and nucleic acids. Discovered as P granules in ",
 StyleBox["C. elegans",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " germ cells (Brangwynne et al., 2009), they have since been found to \
organise virtually every aspect of cellular function: gene regulation, signal \
transduction, stress response, and the formation of structures from the \
nucleolus to synaptic densities."
}], "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"dc646665-0c91-4b76-9cf2-bd4f4ed868d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This notebook develops the mathematical physics of condensates from first \
principles. We implement the ",
 StyleBox["Flory\[Dash]Huggins",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " free energy to derive the phase diagram, solve the ",
 StyleBox["Cahn\[Dash]Hilliard",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " partial differential equation for spinodal decomposition, compute the ",
 StyleBox["concentration enhancement",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " that makes condensates natural chemical reactors, and model the ",
 StyleBox["protocell dynamics",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (growth, division, competition) that connect condensates to the origin of \
life. We conclude with the ",
 StyleBox["liquid \[Rule] gel \[Rule] aggregate",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " transition that links condensate dysfunction to neurodegenerative \
disease."
}], "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"0ff19526-dd47-4fab-90f6-38e8add37f11"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Audience:",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the prose is written for two overlapping audiences. Each section opens \
with an intuitive explanation that requires no background, then deepens into \
a quantitative treatment with equations, numerical integration, and \
visualisations. Biophysicists will recognise the canonical references; \
readers from other backgrounds should be able to follow the physical \
narrative."
}], "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"ad2fc163-2504-47ee-8236-f8a3e3dec2c6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "All code and figures are original and open-source: ",
 StyleBox["github.com/mthiel74/biomolecular-condensates",
  FontWeight->"SemiBold"],
 " (",
 StyleBox["https://github.com/mthiel74/biomolecular-condensates",
  FontFamily->"Courier",
  FontSize->10],
 ")",
 "."
}], "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"7dd7d9c9-98ef-4dbf-aa3d-df78259cdcc1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Roadmap. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\[Section]2\[Dash]3 build the equilibrium and dynamical theory \
(Flory\[Dash]Huggins phase diagrams, Cahn\[Dash]Hilliard spinodal \
decomposition and coarsening). \[Section]4\[Dash]6 turn condensates into \
chemistry: concentration enhancement, an RNA-world replication window, and \
protocell growth, division and proto-Darwinian selection. \[Section]7 covers \
the liquid\[Rule]gel\[Rule]aggregate disease transition. \[Section]8\[Dash]10 \
add the nonlinear-dynamics toolkit (stability, bifurcation, Lyapunov \
functionals), active/chemically-maintained condensates, and the emergent \
layer where selection, Turing patterns and wet\[Dash]dry cycles arise. \
\[Section]11 concludes."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2ae96f5c-505b-4a5d-8f51-13bf90419534"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Initialisation \[LongDash] evaluate this cell first. It loads the figure \
package ",
 StyleBox["condensate_figures.wl",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " from the ",
 StyleBox["same folder",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " as this notebook (keep the two files together). Every figure below is then \
generated by the code cell shown just above it."
}], "Text",
 FontSize->12,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.4],ExpressionUUID->"552a4a1b-d887-454e-b6ce-8bce4bb84fb3"],

