Cell["\<\
Figure 8.2  Fastest-growing wavelength \[Lambda]* over the (\[Phi]\:2080, \
\[Kappa]) plane (clipped at 25 for contrast). The white curve is the spinodal \
f\[Prime]\[Prime] = 0; outside it the homogeneous state is linearly stable \
and no length scale is selected.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"4fe4f84d-a5af-4012-9d72-3f7332c5b9b6"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
8.3  Bifurcation: common-tangent coexistence vs. the spinodal\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5da88b00-f019-4797-83be-51b475e7e541"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sweeping the control parameter traces out the ",
 StyleBox["bifurcation diagram",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ". For the symmetric double well ",
 StyleBox["f = -a/2\[ThinSpace]\[Phi]\.b2 + b/4\[ThinSpace]\[Phi]\:2074",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the coexistence amplitude follows a supercritical pitchfork: the binodal \
",
 StyleBox["\[Phi] = \[PlusMinus]sqrt(a/b)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " encloses the spinodal ",
 StyleBox["\[Phi] = \[PlusMinus]sqrt(a/3b)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ". For Flory\[Dash]Huggins the coexistence curve is the ",
 StyleBox["common-tangent",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (Maxwell) construction. Because the osmotic pressure is linear in \[Chi], \
the dense branch follows the closed form ",
 StyleBox["\[Chi](\[Phi]_R) = (\[Phi]_R g(\[Phi]_R) - h(\[Phi]_R))/\[Phi]_R\
\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", which is numerically robust where the repository's earlier two-variable \
solver failed."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6542015d-73f1-41bf-a2d0-3c286364d234"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figNLPhaseDiagram", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
