 CellLabel->
  " Out[24]=",ExpressionUUID->"a901d47b-f4be-40b6-b78c-7edbe653024c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 8.5  Mass-conserving rate enhancement ",
 StyleBox["k_eff/k_out",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ". (a) Dependence on the partition coefficients at fixed dense fraction p = \
0.05. (b) Dependence on dense fraction for several K: each curve peaks at p* \
\[TildeTilde] 1/K with a maximum gain of order K/4, far below the open-system \
K\.b2."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"60384fb6-34ef-4e7a-b77d-247e2fee18a3"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.  Active and chemically-maintained condensates", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3755021a-ac1d-430a-9c6d-278430edaff8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Living condensates are not at equilibrium: ATP-driven reactions continually \
build up and break down their components. This section extends the model with \
chemistry. Code: ",
 StyleBox["src/active_models.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["src/fh_extensions.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", and ",
 StyleBox["wolfram/active_dynamics.wls",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"21e4d599-8d42-4e7c-bee5-20e2fc42643d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.1  Reaction-arrested coarsening", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"851030f4-efab-4241-a353-d152d6651410"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Add a linear chemical reaction that interconverts droplet material and a \
soluble form, ",
 StyleBox["s(\[Phi]) = k_+(1-\[Phi]) - k_-\[Phi] = -k_react(\[Phi]-\[Phi]_ss)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", to the conserved dynamics:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fd5b9724-501e-4eeb-8afa-a0c413d577b5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "\[Phi]"}], 
    RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "t"}]], "=", "M", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[Del]", "2"], "\[Mu]", "-", 
   SubscriptBox["k", "react"], 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"\[Phi]", "-", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "ss"]}], ")"}]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellMargins->{{80, 50}, {8, 
  8}},ExpressionUUID->"be68afdd-1c64-4bfd-8c27-192e5f788aba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The reaction adds a uniform ",
 StyleBox["-k_react",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " to the growth rate, ",
 StyleBox["\[Omega](k) = -Mk\.b2(f\[Prime]\[Prime]+\[Kappa]k\.b2) - k_react",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", which ",
 StyleBox["stabilises the long-wavelength modes",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 ": the unstable band becomes finite and a length scale is selected. Ostwald \
ripening is arrested and the system settles into a steady-state emulsion \
\[LongDash] the mechanism behind chemically-active droplets (Zwicker et al. \
2015; Bauermann et al. 2025)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7ab4cb95-1e33-404c-8583-3f9457c93401"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figActiveDispersion", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  " In[25]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f9bd0083-15ed-471a-a2b5-1bf9fd76a91f"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
Legended[-Graphics-, Placed[LineLegend[{Directive[Opacity[1.], 
 
>       AbsoluteThickness[2], Thickness[Large], RGBColor[0., 0., 0.]], 
 
>      Directive[Opacity[1.], AbsoluteThickness[2], Thickness[Large], 
 
>       RGBColor[0.788287, 0.259816, 0.270778]], 
 
>      Directive[Opacity[1.], AbsoluteThickness[2], Thickness[Large], 
 
>       RGBColor[1., 0.682688, 0.129771]], 
 
>      Directive[Opacity[1.], AbsoluteThickness[2], Thickness[Large], 
 
>       RGBColor[1., 1., 1.]]}, 
 
>     {k      = 0., k      = 0.05, k      = 0.15, k      = 0.25}, 
        react        react          react          react
 
>     LegendMarkers -> None, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> Column], 
 
>    {0.25, 0.28}, Identity]]\
\>"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.991475494795959*^9},
 CellLabel->
  " Out[25]=",ExpressionUUID->"0d0fae55-d0ca-457b-99b5-4c0766e08701"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Figure 9.1  Reaction-modified dispersion relation. Increasing the reaction \
rate pushes the small-k (long-wavelength) modes below zero, leaving a finite \
unstable band \[LongDash] coarsening can no longer proceed to arbitrarily \
large domains.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"8cc0f334-dd0e-41cb-a418-783041b9d340"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figReaction1D", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  " In[26]:=",ExpressionUUID->"786ae34e-1e00-4220-9b74-fbecd337b904"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
-Graphics-\
\>"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.991475496584214*^9},
 CellLabel->
  " Out[26]=",ExpressionUUID->"f721d557-d2a3-495e-872a-a6b0d48e782d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Figure 9.2  1D reaction\[Dash]Cahn\[Dash]Hilliard (NDSolve). (a) Without \
reaction the domains coarsen toward a single domain. (b) With reaction the \
pattern freezes into a steady-state periodic structure of selected wavelength.\
\>", "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"186a104c-38f6-463a-b8ae-7f513b79b907"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The full 2D problem (solved with a spectral method in ",
 StyleBox["src/active_models.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ") sharpens the same picture: chemical turnover turns the coarse, \
ever-growing morphology into a fine ",
 StyleBox["steady-state emulsion",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " whose mean droplet size shrinks with reaction rate, and whose size \
distribution is narrower than the passive LSW one (Bauermann et al. 2025)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0ccf7b1e-b520-4e18-88e9-d1a75351f728"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9.2  Active Model B: broken detailed balance", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d3c9c4d8-bca0-40bd-9805-637ad9912937"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A genuinely non-equilibrium term ",
 StyleBox["\[Lambda]|\[Del]\[Phi]|\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " added to the chemical potential breaks detailed balance (Active Model B; \
Tjhung et al. 2018). Measured honestly, this term shifts the coexistence \
densities ",
 StyleBox["asymmetrically",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (the dense phase becomes denser than the dilute phase is dilute) and \
modestly slows coarsening, but does ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " by itself arrest it \[LongDash] the robust route to a steady-state \
emulsion is the chemical reaction of \[Section]9.1."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"31846dcb-28e8-443c-a593-cf5188c99364"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
9.3  Stickers and spacers: multivalency drives phase separation\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"32254cfe-d0db-470b-ae04-5c0ff06807c9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Real biomolecules interact through specific, saturable contacts (\"stickers\
\" joined by flexible \"spacers\"; Harmon & Pappu 2017). Adding a saturable \
association free energy ",
 StyleBox["f_bond = \[Phi]_s [ln(1-p)+p/2]",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (bond fraction ",
 StyleBox["p",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " from the law of mass action ",
 StyleBox["p/(1-p)\.b2 = K_a \[Phi]_s",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["\[Phi]_s = v\[Phi]",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ") to the Flory\[Dash]Huggins free energy expands the two-phase region and \
lowers the critical interaction: higher sticker valence ",
 StyleBox["v",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " makes phase separation far easier."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c902a93d-79e1-4046-8232-7f0d90414445"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figStickers", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  " In[27]:=",ExpressionUUID->"98f1484d-b7f3-4d41-9f8f-9356bc52a864"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
                                                             1
