Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.  Emergent complexity: selection, patterns and cycles", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"91b02945-0ce3-4539-9d8d-27c999262497"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The final layer of the model lets genuinely life-like behaviour emerge from \
the same physics. Code: ",
 StyleBox["src/multicomponent.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["src/darwinian_selection.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["src/reaction_diffusion_cargo.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["src/wet_dry_cycling.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["src/parameter_space.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", and the Wolfram companion ",
 StyleBox["wolfram/phase3_extensions.wls",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aa105ec8-1eb3-495b-a1f6-beb236d59e95"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.1  Multi-component condensates", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"09d6280a-a553-48ea-9b33-b5b7ac035e90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Real condensates contain dozens of macromolecules. For ",
 StyleBox["N",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " mutually attracting components that co-condense in near-stoichiometric \
proportions, the demixing entropy is reduced as if they were one effective \
polymer of length ",
 StyleBox["N",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", and the symmetric Flory\[Dash]Huggins critical point migrates (Qian & \
Knowles 2022):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36259999-845e-4b33-a9cb-acab4093032a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[Phi]", "c"], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", 
    RowBox[{"1", "+", 
     SqrtBox["N"]}]], ",", "\[InvisibleSpace]", "\[InvisibleSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox["\[Chi]", "c"], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"2", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{"(", "1", "+", 
       SqrtBox["N"], ")"}], "2"]}], "N"]}], 
  TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellMargins->{{80, 50}, {8, 
  8}},ExpressionUUID->"3096f0da-631b-4e9f-b8c9-55823762094a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As ",
 StyleBox["N",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " grows the critical concentration falls toward zero \[LongDash] multivalent \
mixtures phase-separate at vanishing concentration \[LongDash] and the \
critical interaction drops, so they demix far more easily. Distinct scaffolds \
give distinct condensates, and each client partitions selectively into the \
one it binds best (the physical basis of organelle identity)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6aa41f2e-5e64-4622-9d9e-d8addd3697d7"],

