Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.3  Reaction-diffusion inside condensates", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"bc7dcb4c-3877-4be3-8804-2dceec0cbe25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A condensate is also a chemical reactor. When crowding slows the activator \
far more than the inhibitor, the diffusion ratio ",
 StyleBox["D_v/D_u",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " crosses the ",
 StyleBox["Turing threshold",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ",
 StyleBox["only inside",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " the dense phase: a band of wavenumbers becomes unstable there while every \
mode stays stable in the dilute surroundings, so spots self-organise inside \
the condensate and nowhere else. (The full 2D patterns, and the reaction \
hotspot that forms in a shell at the droplet interface, are computed in ",
 StyleBox["src/reaction_diffusion_cargo.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4eed9ffd-6ded-49a0-b50b-14e70053e00c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figTuring", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  " In[34]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2f6b1324-e8d1-4e28-a064-d071c992197b"],

