}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 10.5  Schnakenberg linear-stability growth rate ",
 StyleBox["\[Lambda](k)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ": inside the dense phase a band of wavenumbers is unstable (patterns form), \
while in the dilute phase every mode is stable. The Turing instability is \
switched on by the condensate."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"0326b0d4-9139-4200-8f92-f2449961728c"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.4  Wet-dry cycling", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"4efab9c6-2ea9-4ae3-8402-a91d158f673b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the early Earth, rock pools cycled between flooded (wet) and evaporated \
(dry) states. Cycling the interaction ",
 StyleBox["\[Chi](t)=\[Chi]_0+\[CapitalDelta]\[Chi] sin(2\[Pi]t/T)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " swings the system between a one-phase well (dissolve, remix) and a \
spinodally unstable double well (re-nucleate many droplets). Each dissolution \
erases the size differences that drive Ostwald ripening, so a ",
 StyleBox["population",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " of droplets is maintained, while a matched constant-",
 StyleBox["\[Chi]",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " run coarsens toward a single winner (Ianeselli 2022)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"58ee6f96-7157-4866-a15e-eabf3884378f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"figWetDry", "[", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  " In[35]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ab17b57c-bf5b-41b5-b53c-c234a1a9d495"],

Cell[OutputFormData["\<\
Legended[-Graphics-, Placed[BarLegend[{Blend[RedBlueTones, #1] & , 
 
          69   69
>      {-(--), --}}, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> Column, 
          50   50
 
>     LegendMarkerSize -> 408., ScalingFunctions -> {Identity, Identity}, 
 
>     Charting`AxisLabel -> None, Charting`TickSide -> Right, 
 
>     ColorFunctionScaling -> True], After, Identity]]\
\>"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.99147550089126*^9},
 CellLabel->
  " Out[35]=",ExpressionUUID->"7f819fa4-db88-4388-918c-316c5756fc56"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Figure 10.6  1D wet\[Dash]dry Cahn\[Dash]Hilliard space\[Dash]time (",
 StyleBox["NDSolve",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "): with a cyclic well depth ",
 StyleBox["a(t)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", domains dissolve at each wet half-cycle and re-nucleate at each dry \
half-cycle. The repeated dissolution resets the size differences that would \
otherwise drive Ostwald ripening, so a population of droplets is sustained \
rather than coarsening to a single winner (Ianeselli et al. 2022)."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{70, 70}, {2, 14}},
 FontSize->11,
 FontSlant->Italic,
 FontColor->GrayLevel[
  0.35],ExpressionUUID->"f17e45cf-8d6f-4638-90cb-2c714d5661bd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["10.5  The accessible parameter space", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"cebff65e-b10f-470c-90d3-06fd90071148"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finally, two analytic maps of the model's regimes: the ",
 StyleBox["(\[Chi],N)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " plane separating one-phase from two-phase by the critical line ",
 StyleBox["\[Chi]_c(N)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", and the ",
 StyleBox["(K,p)",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " mass-conserving rate-enhancement landscape with its optimal ridge ",
 StyleBox["p*\[TildeTilde]1/K",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ". (The full four-panel regime atlas \[LongDash] which also includes the \
thermodynamic ",
 StyleBox["(\[Phi]_0,\[Kappa])",
  FontFamily->"Times",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " plane and the active dissolution / microphase / macrophase plane from 2D \
simulations \[LongDash] is built in ",
 StyleBox["src/parameter_space.py",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02583063-f357-4d51-8c8a-96e31c9f80d5"],

