Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["11.  Conclusions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bdd0fac6-5235-4493-b2e7-80f35e3f4e78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["What we showed.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " (1) The Flory\[Dash]Huggins lattice theory, implemented in a few lines of \
Wolfram Language, correctly predicts the qualitative phase behaviour of \
biomolecular condensates: a UCST phase diagram with the critical \
concentration shifting to lower values for longer/more multivalent molecules. \
(2) The Cahn\[Dash]Hilliard equation, solved natively by ",
 StyleBox["NDSolve",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", captures spinodal decomposition; the subsequent Lifshitz\[Dash]Slyozov t\
\[ThinSpace]^(1/3) coarsening is reproduced with the double-well Model B \
form, since the stiff Flory\[Dash]Huggins solver freezes near the pure \
phases. (3) The concentration-enhancement argument gives a K\.b2 boost for \
bimolecular reactions in the open-system limit \[LongDash] a partial \
resolution of the dilute-ocean problem, since mass conservation caps the \
realised gain at order K/4 (\[Section]8.5). (4) Protocell simulations show \
that condensate populations can undergo proto-Darwinian selection without \
genetic material. (5) The liquid\[Dash]to\[Dash]gel\[Dash]to\[Dash]aggregate \
transition connects condensate physics to neurodegenerative disease. (6) \
Layering the model \[LongDash] multi-component mixtures, a replicating cargo \
with heredity and a shared nutrient, reaction-diffusion, and wet-dry cycling \
\[LongDash] makes genuinely life-like behaviour emerge: ",
 StyleBox["natural selection, Turing morphogenesis, and ripening-resistant \
droplet populations all fall out of the same physics.",
  FontWeight->Bold]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"757fb8ed-ae2a-4877-8c06-6e3637b0350d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The bigger picture.",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " Biomolecular condensates sit at the intersection of soft-matter physics, \
molecular biology, the origin of life, and neurodegeneration. The \
mathematical framework \[LongDash] Flory\[Dash]Huggins thermodynamics, Cahn\
\[Dash]Hilliard dynamics, Michaelis\[Dash]Menten kinetics, \
Lifshitz\[Dash]Slyozov coarsening \[LongDash] is classical and \
well-understood. What is new is the recognition that this physics operates \
inside living cells, that it provides the thermodynamic foundation for \
protocellular compartments, and that its failure modes are disease. The \
condensate revolution is not a discovery of new physics; it is the discovery \
that old physics was hiding in plain sight inside biology."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00158438-089f-4287-a875-51eb17e8add6"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["Key takeaways.",
 FontWeight->Bold]], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cf7f51cf-8db2-43c6-86d8-3c10b20b7c22"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Phase separation is thermodynamics, not biology. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "A two-parameter Flory\[Dash]Huggins free energy already predicts when \
proteins and RNA demix into condensates."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2c498461-47e5-4ea3-bffa-760cb588eaf2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Concentration is the payoff \[LongDash] but it is bounded. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Partitioning boosts bimolecular rates by up to K\.b2 in the open-system \
limit, while mass conservation caps the realised gain at order K/4."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"416c2bf5-b3d6-417f-9ec2-03dcdc9e3649"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Life-like behaviour is emergent. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Add chemistry, heredity and a shared resource and natural selection, Turing \
patterns and ripening-resistant populations fall out of the same equations \
\[LongDash] no biology hand-coded."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"187d086c-c8c0-4cba-9504-fa37e4068c0b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The same physics, run backwards, is disease. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "The liquid\[Rule]gel\[Rule]solid maturation that endangers neurons is the \
flip side of the transition that organises healthy cells."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"9e1cbea4-9cf0-48c2-90d9-4e343c182682"]
}, Open  ]],

